# Documentation Standards

## Code Comments

### Class Documentation
```cpp
/**
 * @brief Downloads a file from multiple sources using P2P protocols
 *
 * This class manages the complete lifecycle of a file download,
 * including source discovery, connection management, and integrity
 * verification through hashing.
 *
 * @note Thread-safe for read operations, write operations require external synchronization
 */
class CDownloadTask {
    // ...
};
```

### Function Documentation
```cpp
/**
 * @brief Starts the download process
 *
 * Initiates connections to available sources and begins
 * transferring file chunks. The download may be resumed
 * if partially complete.
 *
 * @return true if download started successfully, false otherwise
 *
 * @throws std::runtime_error if initialization fails
 * @throws NetworkException if no sources available
 *
 * @note This method is thread-safe
 */
bool Start();

/**
 * @brief Cancels the active download
 *
 * Stops all active transfers and releases resources.
 * The download can be resumed later if desired.
 *
 * @note This method may block briefly while cleaning up connections
 */
void Cancel();
```

### Parameter Documentation
```cpp
/**
 * @brief Processes a network packet
 *
 * @param pBuffer Pointer to packet data (must not be null)
 * @param nSize Size of packet data in bytes (must be > 0)
 * @param peer Information about the peer that sent the packet
 *
 * @return true if packet processed successfully, false otherwise
 *
 * @throws std::invalid_argument if pBuffer is null or nSize is 0
 */
bool ProcessPacket(const BYTE* pBuffer, size_t nSize, const CPeerInfo& peer);
```

## Inline Comments

### Algorithm Documentation
```cpp
void CDownloadTask::ProcessChunk(const BYTE* pData, size_t nLength) {
    // Verify chunk hash before processing to ensure data integrity
    if (!VerifyChunkHash(pData, nLength)) {
        LogError("Chunk hash verification failed");
        RequestChunkRetry();
        return;
    }

    // Update progress and write to file atomically
    m_nDownloaded += nLength;
    WriteToFile(pData, nLength);

    // Notify observers of progress update (thread-safe)
    NotifyProgress(GetProgressPercent());
}
```

### Complex Logic
```cpp
bool CNetworkManager::FindBestSource(const CString& strHash) {
    // First, check active connections for this hash
    for (auto& connection : m_activeConnections) {
        if (connection.HasHash(strHash)) {
            // Prefer sources with higher bandwidth
            if (connection.GetBandwidth() > MIN_ACCEPTABLE_BANDWIDTH) {
                return true;
            }
        }
    }

    // If no active source found, search in discovered sources
    // Sort by reliability and bandwidth
    auto sources = GetDiscoveredSources(strHash);
    std::sort(sources.begin(), sources.end(),
        [](const auto& a, const auto& b) {
            // Sort by reliability first, then bandwidth
            if (a.GetReliability() != b.GetReliability()) {
                return a.GetReliability() > b.GetReliability();
            }
            return a.GetBandwidth() > b.GetBandwidth();
        });

    return !sources.empty();
}
```

