## Thread Safety Documentation

```cpp
/**
 * @brief Updates download progress
 *
 * @param nPercent Progress percentage (0-100)
 *
 * @note This method is thread-safe and can be called from any thread
 * @note UI updates are automatically dispatched to the main thread
 */
void UpdateProgress(int nPercent);

/**
 * @brief Gets the current download state
 *
 * @return Current download state
 *
 * @note This method is thread-safe for read operations
 * @warning Do not modify state while reading
 */
DownloadState GetState() const;
```

## Ownership and Lifetime Documentation

```cpp
/**
 * @brief Creates a new download connection
 *
 * @param strHost Host address or IP
 * @param nPort Port number
 *
 * @return Pointer to connection object (caller takes ownership)
 *
 * @note Caller is responsible for deleting the returned pointer
 * @note Returns nullptr on failure
 */
CConnection* CreateConnection(const CString& strHost, WORD nPort);

/**
 * @brief Gets the shared application settings
 *
 * @return Reference to settings object
 *
 * @note The returned reference is valid for the lifetime of the application
 * @warning Do not store this reference beyond the current scope
 */
CSettings& GetSettings();
```

## API Documentation

### Public Interface
```cpp
/**
 * @class CDownloadTask
 * @brief Manages file downloads from P2P sources
 *
 * This class provides a high-level interface for downloading files
 * from multiple P2P sources with automatic source management,
 * error recovery, and progress tracking.
 *
 * @example
 * @code
 * CDownloadTask task;
 * task.SetFileName(_T("example.zip"));
 * task.SetHash(strFileHash);
 * if (task.Start()) {
 *     // Download in progress
 * }
 * @endcode
 */
class CDownloadTask {
    // ...
};
```

## Avoid

- Outdated comments that don't match code
- Obvious comments that just repeat the code
- Missing documentation for public APIs
- Not documenting thread safety requirements
- Not documenting ownership semantics
- Comments in languages other than English

## Language Requirements

- **All comments must be in English**
- Code comments, documentation, and commit messages
- Variable names and identifiers should be in English
- Exception: Localization strings and UI text
